      "snippet": "Compute the standard deviation along the specified axis. By default, NumPy uses ddof=0, which means the divisor is N rather than N-1 for the population standard deviation; for example, np.std([1, 2, 3, 4]) returns 1.118033988749895. The documentation also notes that the coefficient of variation is commonly calculated as std/mean, often expressed as a percentage.",
      "domain": "numpy.org",
      "rank": 1
    },
