      "title": "Coefficient of Variation (CV) Formula and Interpretation",
      "url": "https://www.statology.org/coefficient-of-variation-formula/",
      "snippet": "The coefficient of variation is defined as CV = \u03c3 / \u03bc, or s / x\u0304 for sample data, and is usually multiplied by 100 to express a percentage. For a dataset with mean 50 and standard deviation 5, the CV is 10%, which makes it easy to compare variability across different scales.",
      "domain": "statology.org",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Standard Deviation in Python: population vs sample",
      "url": "https://realpython.com/numpy-standard-deviation/",
